.TH WAYBAR-MODS 1 "2026" "waybar-mods" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
waybar-mods \- build Waybar from source with a set of overlay modules and
patches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B setup.sh
[\fBinstall\fR|\fBverify\fR|\fBcheck\fR|\fBuninstall\fR|\fBtest\fR|\
\fBversion\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B waybar-mods
is a Waybar distribution: pristine upstream Waybar (pinned in
.IR refs )
plus a set of custom Cairo modules and behaviour patches, assembled onto a clean
checkout and built from source into a prefix. It is NOT a fork; upstream is
fetched at a known-good tag and the additions are applied as overlays and
patches, so each one stays a discrete, upstreamable unit and the base can be
refreshed by bumping one ref.
.PP
The added modules are a windows taskbar
.RB ( wayfire/taskbar ),
a Cairo line-graph system monitor
.RB ( sysmon/graph ),
brightness/volume/battery gauges
.RB ( hw/gauge ),
an analog clock
.RB ( clock/analog ),
a now-playing card
.RB ( media/card ),
a Bluetooth indicator
.RB ( hw/bluetooth ),
and a next-meeting card
.RB ( cal/card ).
The patches add shared flush tooltips, a hover-zoom magnifier, a stable
config-driven SNI tray order, an SNI property re-fetch, and PulseAudio linkage
for the media card spectrum.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B install
Build and install waybar into the prefix (default
.IR ~/.local ).
Incremental: a no-op when the installed binary already matches the current
overlays, patches, and upstream pin, so it is safe to re-run on every
provision.
.TP
.B verify
Build into a throwaway prefix and discard it, proving the overlays and patches
still apply and compile against the pinned upstream without touching the real
install. This is the check to run while iterating on a module or before bumping
the upstream pin.
.TP
.B check
Report whether waybar is installed, self-contained by rpath, and in sync with
the source, as
.RB [ OK ]/[ FAIL ]
markers.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the installed waybar and the build stamp.
.TP
.B version
Print the package version and the upstream Waybar pin.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I refs
The upstream Waybar URL and pinned ref (the lower of the two-level pin).
.TP
.I overlays/
The custom module sources plus
.IR registration.patch .
.TP
.I patches/
The behaviour patches applied onto the checkout.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/waybar-mods/
The upstream checkout, build tree, and sync stamp.
.SH NOTES
Entirely unprivileged: a user build into a user prefix, no sudo. The installed
binary carries a relative
.RB ( $ORIGIN/../lib )
rpath, so the prefix is self-contained with no ld.so.conf entry.
